#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:176
#, no-c-format
msgid "Solve Crosswords, Download new puzzles and Design your Own"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:190
#, no-c-format
msgid "Library"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:191
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The library is shown after the game has started. If it's not shown, you can "
"always switch back to the library by using the <guilabel>Library</guilabel> "
"tab on top:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:206
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The library shows all your crosswords. In the toolbar of the library you have "
"some options to fill your library: <guilabel>Download</guilabel>, <guilabel>"
"Import</guilabel>, <guilabel>New Crossword</guilabel>"
". There are also options to organize your library: <guilabel>Delete</guilabel>"
" "
"and <guilabel>New Folder</guilabel>. Some buttons need a crossword to be "
"selected."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:221
#, no-c-format
msgid "Downloading Crosswords"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:222
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the library click <guilabel>Download</guilabel> to open the download "
"dialog. "
"Select a <guilabel>provider</guilabel> to show a list of offered crosswords. "
"A "
"preview is shown for the selected crossword. To find a specific crossword you "
"can use the <emphasis>search line</emphasis>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:224
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can change the target folder for downloaded crosswords at the bottom of "
"the "
"download dialog."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:226
#, no-c-format
msgid "Click <guilabel>Ok</guilabel> to download the selected crossword."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:242
#, no-c-format
msgid "Importing Crosswords"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:243
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the library click <guilabel>Import</guilabel> to import local crossword "
"files to your library. You can also add crosswords to the library by dropping "
"files, &eg; from &dolphin;. The following file formats are supported:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:246 index.docbook:258
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>.puz</guilabel> (AcrossLite)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:248 index.docbook:260
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>.kwp</guilabel> (for <guilabel>k</guilabel>ross-<guilabel>w<"
"/guilabel>"
"ord-<guilabel>p</guilabel>uzzle)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:250 index.docbook:262
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>.kwpz</guilabel> (compressed .kwp-files)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:254
#, no-c-format
msgid "Exporting Crosswords"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:255
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the library click <guilabel>Export</guilabel> to export the selected "
"crossword. The following file formats are supported for exporting:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:264
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>.pdf</guilabel> (Acrobat Reader, &okular;, ...)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:266
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>.ps</guilabel> (Post script)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:268 index.docbook:270
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>.png</guilabel> (Image format)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:274
#, no-c-format
msgid "Creating New Crosswords"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:275
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the library click <guilabel>New Crossword</guilabel>"
", which will open a dialog. In the <guilabel>General</guilabel> "
"tab you can choose a crossword type and set some information like the authors "
"name (you) or the size of the crossword. You can also create user defined "
"crossword types. See <link linkend=\"crossword-types\">Crossword Types</link> "
"for an overview of the available crossword types. All settings can be changed "
"later via <menuchoice><guimenu>Edit</guimenu><guimenuitem>"
"Crossword Properties...</guimenuitem></menuchoice>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:290
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the <guilabel>Template</guilabel> tab you can choose to use a template. "
"Templates are complete crosswords, but without clue texts or answer letters. "
"You can use them to quickly create new crosswords by just filling in the "
"clues. "
"If you have a good <link linkend=\"using-the-dictionary\">dictionary</link> "
"this can be really easy."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:292
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can easily create new templates by saving a crossword with the option "
"<guilabel>Save As Template</guilabel> enabled (use <menuchoice><guimenu>"
"Game</guimenu><guimenuitem>Save As</guimenuitem></menuchoice>"
"). If you want the new template to appear in the <guilabel>Create New<"
"/guilabel> "
"dialog you should save it to the default <guilabel>Templates</guilabel> "
"place (which appears in the <guilabel>Save As</guilabel> dialog)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:307
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"After clicking <guilabel>Ok</guilabel> the new crossword is created and shown "
"in edit mode. See <link linkend=\"editing-crosswords\">Editing Crosswords<"
"/link> "
"to see how to edit that new crossword."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:310
#, no-c-format
msgid "Organize your library"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:311
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To delete the selected crossword from the library click <guilabel>"
"Delete</guilabel>. You can also delete a folder from the library. This will "
"delete all contained crosswords in that folder."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:313
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To create new folders click <guilabel>New Folder</guilabel>"
", which will ask you for a name for the new folder."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:315
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can also drag and drop crosswords from one folder of the library to "
"another."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:319
#, no-c-format
msgid "Printing"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:320
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can view a print preview using <menuchoice><guimenu>Game</guimenu>"
"<guimenuitem>Print Preview</guimenuitem></menuchoice>"
". To print a crossword use <menuchoice><guimenu>Game</guimenu><guimenuitem>"
"Print...</guimenuitem></menuchoice>. Besides all the default printing "
"options, "
"you can choose a color for empty cells in <menuchoice><guimenu>Options<"
"/guimenu>"
"<guimenuitem>Crossword</guimenuitem></menuchoice> tab."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:323
#, no-c-format
msgid "Playing Crosswords"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:324
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Choose a crossword to play from the library and then click <guilabel>"
"Open</guilabel> in the toolbar or double click that crossword. See <link "
"linkend=\"library\">Library</link> for instructions on how to add crosswords "
"to "
"your library."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:326
#, no-c-format
msgid "This is how the main window will look after opening the crossword:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:341
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can click each letter cell to set the focus to that cell. When you press "
"a "
"letter key, that letter will be put into the focused cell and the next letter "
"cell of the current clue will be focused. Normally you will start with "
"focusing "
"the first letter cell of a clue and then just write the answer using the "
"keyboard."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:343
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the statusbar there is a progress bar, showing you the percentage of "
"filled "
"letter cells, the solving progress. When you filled in all letter cells you "
"can "
"check your solution using <menuchoice><guimenu>Move</guimenu><guimenuitem>"
"Check</guimenuitem></menuchoice> or the corresponding button in the toolbar. "
"If "
"you want to start again, &ie; clearing all answers, use <menuchoice><guimenu>"
"Move</guimenu><guimenuitem>Clear Answers</guimenuitem></menuchoice>"
". You can also clear answers / letters using the context menu or using the "
"<guilabel>Eraser Tool</guilabel>. The Eraser Tool can be enabled using "
"<menuchoice><guimenu>Move</guimenu><guimenuitem>Eraser</guimenuitem>"
"</menuchoice> or by the corresponding toolbar button. When it's enabled you "
"can "
"clear letter cells by clicking them or clear answers by clicking clue cells "
"(that obviously only works, when clue cells are visible)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:345
#, no-c-format
msgid "Navigation"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:346
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"There are many ways to navigate through the crossword. First you can use the "
"<emphasis>arrow keys</emphasis> to move the focus."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:348
#, no-c-format
msgid "There are other actions for navigation (some have default shortcuts):"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:351
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Select First Letter</guilabel> (default shortcut <keycap>Home<"
"/keycap>"
"), selects the first letter of the current clue"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:353
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Select Last Letter</guilabel> (default shortcut <keycap>End</keycap>"
"), selects the last letter of the current clue"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:355
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Select Clue With Switched Orientation</guilabel> "
"(default shortcut <keycap>Tab</keycap>), selects the clue with a different "
"orientation without selecting another letter"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:357
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Select First Clue</guilabel>, selects the first clue"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:359
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Select Previous Clue</guilabel>, selects the previous clue"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:361
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Select Next Clue</guilabel> (default shortcut &Enter;), selects the "
"next clue"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:363
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Select Last Clue</guilabel>, selects the last clue"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:366
#, no-c-format
msgid "All those actions are listed in the <guilabel>Move</guilabel> menu:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:381
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To change the zoom level you can use the <emphasis>zoom slider</emphasis> "
"in the status bar, use the <guilabel>View</guilabel> "
"menu or hold &Ctrl; and zoom in/out with the mouse wheel. You can show the "
"whole crossword in the window using <menuchoice><guimenu>View</guimenu>"
"<guimenuitem>Fit to page</guimenuitem></menuchoice>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:383
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To pan the view you can enable the pan mode using <menuchoice><guimenu>"
"View</guimenu><guimenuitem>Pan</guimenuitem></menuchoice> "
"or the pan button in the toolbar. In pan mode you can use the mouse to drag "
"the "
"view. You can also pan when not in pan mode by pressing and holding &Ctrl;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:385
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can always <guilabel>Save</guilabel> your current work with all currently "
"filled letters."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:388
#, no-c-format
msgid "Hints, Solving"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:389
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When you're stuck while trying to solve a crossword you can get help. There "
"are "
"different actions for getting help:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:392
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Solve the whole crossword (using <menuchoice><guimenu>Move</guimenu>"
"<guimenuitem>Solve</guimenuitem></menuchoice>)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:394
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Solve a whole clue (using the context menu on a letter cell and then choose "
"<guilabel>Solve Across Clue</guilabel> or <guilabel>Solve Down Clue</guilabel>"
")"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:396
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Solve a single letter (using <menuchoice><guimenu>Move</guimenu><guimenuitem>"
"Hint</guimenuitem></menuchoice> or the context menu on a letter cell and then "
"choose <guilabel>Hint For This Cell</guilabel>)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:400
#, no-c-format
msgid "Clue List"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:401
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The clue list isn't shown for all crossword types by default (&eg; not for "
"Swedish crosswords). You can show/hide it via <menuchoice><guimenu>"
"Settings</guimenu><guimenuitem>Clue List</guimenuitem></menuchoice>"
". It shows a list of all clues of the current crossword with it's current "
"answers. You can click each clue in the list to pan the view to that clue. "
"After clicking a clue you can directly start writing the answer."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:404
#, no-c-format
msgid "Solution Toolbar"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:405
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The solution toolbar is only shown for crosswords that have a <emphasis>"
"solution word</emphasis>. Such crosswords have some special letter cells, "
"namely solution letter cells. Those solution letter cells are marked by "
"parenthesized numbers, indicating their position in the solution word. All "
"solution letters together form the solution word."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:407
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can change the solution letters either in the solution toolbar or in the "
"crossword, they synchronize themselves. You can toggle the solution toolbar "
"via "
"<menuchoice><guimenu>Settings</guimenu><guisubmenu>Toolbars Shown</guisubmenu>"
"<guimenuitem>Solution</guimenuitem></menuchoice>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:411
#, no-c-format
msgid "Editing Crosswords"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:412
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To edit crosswords you first need to enable the edit mode using <menuchoice>"
"<guimenu>Edit</guimenu><guimenuitem>Edit Mode</guimenuitem></menuchoice> "
"or the corresponding button in the toolbar. When you have just created a new "
"crossword using the <guilabel>Create New</guilabel> dialog the edit mode is "
"enabled automatically. In edit mode all correct letters are shown and empty "
"cells are visible and focusable. You can <link linkend=\"navigation\">"
"navigate</link> through the crossword in the same way it's done when the edit "
"mode isn't enabled. Changes to letter cells will change their correct letters "
"(indicated by the blue color of the letters)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:414
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You should fill all correct letters, so that no letter stays blank, otherwise "
"solving won't work correctly."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:416
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When you created a new crossword using a template you just need to fill in "
"the "
"letters and clues and you're done. Otherwise you first need to add clues and "
"images if you want (not all crossword types allow images!)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:418
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Different crossword types have different rules, allow different sets of cell "
"types. You can convert your crossword to any type you want, see <link "
"linkend=\"converting-crosswords\">Converting Crosswords</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:420
#, no-c-format
msgid "Adding Clues, Images"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:421
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To add new clues or images, select an empty cell and then use <menuchoice>"
"<guimenu>Edit</guimenu><guimenuitem>Add Clue</guimenuitem></menuchoice> "
"or <menuchoice><guimenu>Edit</guimenu><guimenuitem>Add Image</guimenuitem>"
"</menuchoice> (which won't be shown if the current crossword type doesn't "
"allow "
"image cells). If the current crossword type allows <guilabel>"
"Double Clue Cells</guilabel>, you can also select a clue cell and then choose "
"<menuchoice><guimenu>Edit</guimenu><guimenuitem>Add Clue</guimenuitem>"
"</menuchoice>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:423
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This will immediately add the clue or image into the crossword with default "
"settings. Read the next sections to see how to change the newly created clue "
"or "
"image."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:426
#, no-c-format
msgid "Changing Clues"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:427
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can change clues using the <guilabel>Current Cell Dock</guilabel>"
". If it's not shown you can enable it with <menuchoice><guimenu>"
"Settings</guimenu><guimenuitem>Show Current Cell Dock</guimenuitem><"
"/menuchoice>"
"."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:429
#, no-c-format
msgid "When you have selected a clue it will look like this:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:444
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can change the clue text and insert special characters using the button "
"on "
"the right of the clue input line."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:446
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The orientation of the clue can be changed to <guilabel>Horizontal</guilabel> "
"or <guilabel>Vertical</guilabel> if that's possible. When it's not possible, "
"it's because the clue is too long for the other orientation or because there "
"are other cells preventing the orientation to be changed (&eg; a clues answer "
"can't cross other clue cells)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:448
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When you have <link linkend=\"managing-the-dictionary\">"
"set up a dictionary</link> the dictionary group box is shown in the <guilabel>"
"Current Cell</guilabel> dock. See <link linkend=\"using-the-dictionary\">"
"Using The Dictionary</link> to see how to use it."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:450
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When the current crossword type allows or requires clue cells to be shown the "
"<guilabel>Current Cell</guilabel> dock includes a group of buttons to change "
"the <emphasis>answer offset</emphasis>. The answer offset is the offset of "
"the "
"first letter cell of the answer to it's clue cell (topleft, top, topright, "
"left, on clue cell, right, bottomleft, bottom, bottomright). American "
"crosswords disallow clue cells, &ie; the answer offset is always 'on clue "
"cell'. Swedish crosswords require clue cells, &ie; the answer offset can't be "
"'on clue cell'."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:452
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<emphasis>Answer lengths</emphasis> can be changed interactively by dragging "
"the bar after the last letter cell of a clue. The answer length is changed by "
"adding / removing letter cells from the clue. You can't make an answer "
"shorter "
"than the minimum allowed answer length of the current crossword type."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:455
#, no-c-format
msgid "Changing images"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:456
#, no-c-format
msgid "TODO"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:459
#, no-c-format
msgid "Converting Crosswords"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:460
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can convert every crossword to every other crossword type. To do this, "
"use "
"<menuchoice><guimenu>Edit</guimenu><guimenuitem>Crossword "
"Properties...</guimenuitem></menuchoice>, click the <guilabel>"
"Crossword Type</guilabel> section and then click the <guilabel>"
"Convert...</guilabel> button. This will open the conversion dialog, where you "
"can choose the crossword type to convert to. On the bottom of the dialog an "
"info line is shown which informs you about cells, that will get removed by "
"the "
"conversion. You can undo each conversion."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:462
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"See <link linkend=\"crossword-types\">Crossword Types</link> "
"for a list of available crossword types."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:465
#, no-c-format
msgid "Managing the Dictionary"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:466
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"First you need to have a <guilabel>MySQL server</guilabel> "
"installed and running."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:469
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can open the dictionary dialog via <menuchoice><guimenu>Settings</guimenu>"
"<guimenuitem>Dictionary...</guimenuitem></menuchoice>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:484
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"On the right of the dialog you can see a list of all words in your "
"dictionary. "
"Each word can have an associated clue text."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:486
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"On the left you can see a toolbox with three sections: <guilabel>"
"Fill Dictionary</guilabel>, <guilabel>Edit</guilabel> and <guilabel>"
"Backup</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:488
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To add words with their clue texts from existing crosswords you can use "
"<guilabel>Extract From Library</guilabel>, which extracts all words from all "
"crosswords in your library or <guilabel>Extract From Crosswords...</guilabel>"
", which lets you choose crossword files to extract words from. You can also "
"add "
"words (without clue texts) from plain text dictionary files using <guilabel>"
"Add Words From Dictionary...</guilabel>. Normally the directories /usr/dict "
"or "
"/usr/share/dict contains such dictionaries."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:490
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To add single words use <guilabel>Add Entry</guilabel> from the <guilabel>"
"Edit</guilabel> section. Change the word directly in the list. To remove all "
"selected words from the dictionary use <guilabel>Remove Selected</guilabel>"
", to clear the dictionary use <guilabel>Clear Dictionary</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:492
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Backup</guilabel> section contains two buttons: <guilabel>"
"Import (CSV)...</guilabel> and <guilabel>Export (CSV)...</guilabel>"
". These can be used to import/export the dictionary to/from comma separated "
"files (CSV). CSV-Files can also be imported into spread sheet applications. "
"You "
"can use those files as backup or to share your dictionary with others."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:495
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using the Dictionary"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: emphasis
#: index.docbook:496
#, no-c-format
msgid "TODO: More description of adding clues using the dictionary"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:498
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the <guilabel>Current Cell</guilabel> dock, you can search for matching "
"answers using wildcard patterns (? for one arbitrary letter, * for any number "
"of arbitrary letters). Those patterns are automatically generated based on "
"the "
"letters that are already in the crossword. Therefore matching answers are "
"automatically offered when adding new clues."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:503
#, no-c-format
msgid "Customize - change your Settings"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:517
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To open the settings dialog use <menuchoice><guimenu>Settings</guimenu>"
"<guimenuitem>Configure KrossWordPuzzle...</guimenuitem></menuchoice>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:519
#, no-c-format
msgid "Animations"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:520
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can <guilabel>disable animations</guilabel> if the game is running slow "
"or "
"if you don't like them."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:535
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can enable/disable all animations with <guilabel>"
"Enable Animations</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:537
#, no-c-format
msgid "The other checkboxes enable/disable single animation types:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:540
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Animate Size Changes</guilabel>: Animates changes to the size of "
"image cells."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:542
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Animate Position Changes</guilabel>: Animates changes to the "
"position "
"of cells, &ie; moves the cells to their new position."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:544
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Animate Items Appearance</guilabel>: Fades in new cells."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:546
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Animate Items Disappearance</guilabel>: Fades out cells when they "
"disappear."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:548
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Animate Focus In</guilabel>: Animates cells when they get focus."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:550
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Animate Changing Letter</guilabel>: Turns letter cells around when "
"their letter changes, with the new letter on the other side."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:552
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Animate Changes to an Items Appearance</guilabel>"
": Fades from the previous appearance of a cell to it's new appearance. This "
"also animates selection changes."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:556
#, no-c-format
msgid "Themes"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:557
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>KrossWordPuzzle</guilabel> uses the default theme selection page. "
"Just select the theme you want to use. By default, there are three themes:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:560
#, no-c-format
msgid "Default"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:562
#, no-c-format
msgid "Egyptian"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:564
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Scribble</guilabel> (looks like a handwritten crossword)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:569
#, no-c-format
msgid "Understanding the Puzzle Types"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:583
#, no-c-format
msgid "American Crosswords"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:584
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Crossword grids such as those appearing in most <emphasis>"
"North American</emphasis> newspapers and magazines feature solid areas of "
"white "
"squares. Every letter is checked, and usually each answer is required to "
"contain at least three letters. In such puzzles shaded squares are "
"traditionally limited to about one-sixth of the design. Crossword grids "
"elsewhere, such as in <emphasis>Britain</emphasis> and <emphasis>"
"Australia</emphasis>, have a lattice-like structure, with a higher percentage "
"of shaded squares, leaving up to half the letters in an answer unchecked. For "
"example, if the top row has an answer running all the way across, there will "
"be "
"no across answers in the second row."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:586
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Another tradition in puzzle design (in <emphasis>North America</emphasis> "
"and <emphasis>Britain</emphasis> particularly) is that the grid should have "
"180-degree rotational symmetry, so that its pattern appears the same if the "
"paper is turned upside down. Most puzzle designs also require that all white "
"cells be orthogonally contiguous (that is, connected in one mass through "
"shared "
"sides, to form a single polyomino)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:589
#, no-c-format
msgid "Swedish Crosswords"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:590
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The Swedish-Style grid uses no clue numbers - the clues are contained in the "
"cells which would normally be black in other countries. Arrows indicate in "
"which direction the clues have to be answered, vertical or horizontal. This "
"style of grid is used in several countries other than Sweden, usually in "
"magazines with pages of A4 or similar size. The grid often has a photo of a "
"pop "
"or movie star replacing a block of squares, as a clue to one answer. These "
"puzzles usually have no symmetry in the grid."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:592
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Crosswords with clue cells inside the crossword grid are also called <"
"emphasis>"
"Arrowwords</emphasis>, <emphasis>Pointers</emphasis> or <emphasis>"
"Tipwords</emphasis> in English, <emphasis>Autodefinidos</emphasis> "
"in Spanish, <emphasis>Mots Fléchés</emphasis> in French, etc."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:595
#, no-c-format
msgid "Crossnumbers"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:596
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A <emphasis>crossnumber</emphasis> (also known as a cross-figure) is the "
"numerical analogy of a crossword, in which the solutions to the clues are "
"numbers instead of words. Clues are usually arithmetical expressions, but can "
"also be general knowledge clues to which the answer is a number or year. "
"There "
"are also numerical fill-in crosswords."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:598
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <emphasis>Daily Mail Weekend</emphasis> magazine used to feature "
"crossnumbers under the misnomer <emphasis>Number Word</emphasis>"
". This kind of puzzle should not be confused with a different puzzle that the "
"<emphasis>Daily Mail</emphasis> refers to as <emphasis>Cross Number</emphasis>"
"."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:601
#, no-c-format
msgid "Number Puzzles"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:602
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Number puzzles are a variant of crosswords in which each cell has a number "
"between 1 and 26. The solver has to find out for which letter of the alphabet "
"a "
"number stands."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:605
#, no-c-format
msgid "Free Crosswords"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:606
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This is a special type that tries to be least restrictive. You can use all "
"available cell types (&eg; <emphasis>clue cells</emphasis>, <emphasis>"
"double clue cells</emphasis>, <emphasis>image cells</emphasis>, <emphasis>"
"solution letter cells</emphasis>). You can mix answers that have a clue cell "
"with answers that don't. Answers may contain characters as well as numbers."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:609
#, no-c-format
msgid "User Defined Crosswords"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:610
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Lets you specify your own rules. <guilabel>TODO: Description of the "
"rules</guilabel>"
msgstr ""

